      "content": "#define _GNU_SOURCE\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n#define IBLOCK 4\n#define JBLOCK 128\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nvoid body_force(float *restrict px, float *restrict py, float *restrict pz,\n                float *restrict vx, float *restrict vy, float *restrict vz,\n                float dt, int n) {\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic,64)\n    for (int ib = 0; ib < n; ib += IBLOCK) {\n        int imax = ib + IBLOCK;\n        if (imax > n) imax = n;\n\n        float fx[IBLOCK];\n        float fy[IBLOCK];\n        float fz[IBLOCK];\n        for (int i = 0; i < imax - ib; ++i) {\n            fx[i] = 0.0f;\n            fy[i] = 0.0f;\n            fz[i] = 0.0f;\n        }\n\n        for (int jb = 0; jb < n; jb += JBLOCK) {\n            int jmax = jb + JBLOCK;\n            if (jmax > n) jmax = n;\n\n            for (int i = ib; i < imax; ++i) {\n                float xi = px[i];\n                float yi = py[i];\n                float zi = pz[i];\n                int li = i - ib;\n                float fxi = fx[li];\n                float fyi = fy[li];\n                float fzi = fz[li];\n\n                #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fxi,fyi,fzi) aligned(px,py,pz:16)\n                for (int j = jb; j < jmax; ++j) {\n                    float dx = px[j] - xi;\n                    float dy = py[j] - yi;\n                    float dz = pz[j] - zi;\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n                    fxi += dx * inv_dist3;\n                    fyi += dy * inv_dist3;\n                    fzi += dz * inv_dist3;\n                }\n\n                fx[li] = fxi;\n                fy[li] = fyi;\n                fz[li] = fzi;\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int i = ib; i < imax; ++i) {\n            int li = i - ib;\n            vx[i] += dt * fx[li];\n            vy[i] += dt * fy[li];\n            vz[i] += dt * fz[li];\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  float *px, *py, *pz, *vx, *vy, *vz;\n  posix_memalign((void**)&px,  16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&py,  16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&pz,  16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&vx,  16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&vy,  16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&vz,  16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    px[i] = bodies[i].x;\n    py[i] = bodies[i].y;\n    pz[i] = bodies[i].z;\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\n  }\n\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n    body_force(px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz, DT, nbodies);\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n      px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n      py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n      pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    bodies[i].x = px[i];\n    bodies[i].y = py[i];\n    bodies[i].z = pz[i];\n    bodies[i].vx = vx[i];\n    bodies[i].vy = vy[i];\n    bodies[i].vz = vz[i];\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(px); free(py); free(pz); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n  free(bodies);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining SoA layout with aligned allocation and restrict qualifiers from source B, tiling (IBLOCK=4, JBLOCK=128) from source A, dynamic scheduling on outer i-blocks from source C, plus SIMD reduction pragma on inner j-loops will improve cache locality, enable vectorization, reduce memory traffic, and maintain thread-level parallelism to achieve further speedup beyond any individual transformation.",
  "notes": "Integrated all three sources: SoA layout with aligned allocation (B), tiling of i/j loops (A), dynamic(64) schedule on force loop (C). Added restrict qualifiers and SIMD reduction pragma. Position update parallelized with static schedule. Output matches reference by copying back to Body array before writing.",
